  "mn35:11.3": "",
  "mn35:11.4": "Saccaka is here attempting to appeal to the prejudices of his audience, a cheap debater’s trick.",
  "mn35:11.5": "",
  "mn35:11.6": "",
  "mn35:11.7": "",
  "mn35:11.8": "",
  "mn35:12.1": "",
  "mn35:12.2": "",
  "mn35:12.3": "",
  "mn35:12.4": "Again, Saccaka is trying to appeal to the vanity of his audience. He doesn’t realize, however, that he is setting himself up for a trap. By tying his audience’s vanity to the Buddha’s analogy, he cannot later deny that the analogy is valid.",
